      "supported": "Stage 2 adds staging work with little improvement in readiness. Stage 4 provides enough lookahead to offset that cost and substantially improves the fixed-launch graph benchmark.",
      "evidence": [
        "Stage 2 adds 44.1% executed instructions and 40,960 shared-load wavefronts, with effectively unchanged L2 reads, zero DRAM reads, unchanged block limits and unchanged achieved occupancy.",
        "Stage 4 has the same shared-load wavefront count as stage 2 and only 3.5% more instructions. Eligible warps rise from 0.06 to 0.15 and long-scoreboard stalls per issue fall from 11.43 to 2.36.",
        "Graph timing changes from about 8.40 us baseline to 9.62 us at stage 2 and 4.36 us at stage 4. The same direction holds at eight warps.",
        "Forcing ca is neutral because the original async copies already use ca."
      ],
