  "limitations": [
    "Performance claims use graph timings. Profiler duration can disagree in ranking: upsample stage 3 is faster than baseline in Nsight but slower in all graph confirmations.",
    "Clocks were uncontrolled and no clock-frequency metric was collected. Clock or launch-regime differences could contribute to profile/graph discrepancies, but were not demonstrated.",
    "Short-kernel multi-pass counters are diagnostic. Rotary baseline L2 hits (83,987) slightly exceed read sectors (83,979); do not interpret the derived hit rate literally.",
    "Stall values are per issued instruction, not percentages of elapsed time. A changed instruction denominator and overlapping warp stalls preclude additive runtime attribution.",
    "Long scoreboard denotes L1TEX dependencies and does not by itself establish DRAM bandwidth pressure. Short scoreboard includes shared loads and other MIO operations.",
    "Ordinary global-load sectors are not sufficient to account for all asynchronous traffic. Conclusions about memory traffic use L2 sectors and DRAM bytes alongside saved code.",
    "NCU per-block shared-memory figures and compiler user-shared-memory figures differ by 1,024 bytes in these captures; they are distinct resource measures.",
    "The interventions preserve the computation and required synchronization, but do not isolate synchronization cost from address/control instruction cost or shared-memory loads."
  ],
